WP10.7 -- the one hunk this work package needs in src/XSSet.cpp, NOT APPLIED.

WHY IT IS A FILE AND NOT A COMMIT.  src/XSSet.cpp and src/XSSet.h are being
edited concurrently by WP21-B/C (the FlatXs/XsRecon accessor side).  Two agents
editing one file is how a merge eats a hunk nobody notices is gone, so this one
is handed over instead of applied.  It is not load-bearing for WP10.7: the
admission door in src/Driver.h (establishDeviceResidency) already raises with
the backend's own status BEFORE this seam is reached, so under
RASBERY_GPU_FULL=1 a case that cannot establish flat-XS residency now dies at
the door with the real reason.  This hunk fixes the OTHER half -- the gate-OFF
arm and the mid-run decline, where the door said `ready` at admission and the
device declined a call later on.

WHAT IS WRONG WITH THE LINE TODAY.  It is the seam describing itself.  The four
238 GPU1 arm-A deaths (build 0054838, generations 6/9/12 `promote` and 19 case
14) all carried, byte for byte:

    [RASBERY][GPU_FULL][VIOLATION] subsystem=flatxs site=XSSet::UpdateFlatXS
    reason=the FlatXS device arm declined; the reference reconstruction loop
    runs

which says the arm declined and not why, while XsReconBackend::status() held
the answer one dereference away ("no CUDA device: ...", "stream: ...", "scalar
buffer allocation failed", "cudaMalloc(...) -> ...").  The status reached a
human exactly once per PROCESS, through the std::call_once warn in
TryUpdateFlatXSGpu -- so in a resident evaluator spanning twenty generations the
first case to hit it printed a reason and the other three printed nothing.

WHAT THE HUNK COSTS.  One std::string built on a path that was already about to
run the whole CPU reconstruction loop, and only when the arm is on and the
device declined.  Nothing on the steady path.

THE call_once WARN IS DELIBERATELY LEFT ALONE.  Making it per case would put a
second copy of the same fact in the log; the admission door's
[RASBERY][RESIDENCY] line is already per case and carries the same string.

--- a/src/XSSet.cpp
+++ b/src/XSSet.cpp
@@ -3438,10 +3438,20 @@
             // Device arm declined: fall through to the reference loop.
             // WP1 (plan Sec 6.3).  This seam had no counter of any kind: a
             // FlatXS arm that refused every node looked exactly like an arm
             // that was never set.
-            RASBERY_GPU_FULL_GUARD_IF(rasberyGpuFlatXsEnabled() && !dump_this, FlatXs,
-                                      "XSSet::UpdateFlatXS",
-                                      "the FlatXS device arm declined; the reference "
-                                      "reconstruction loop runs");
+            // WP10.7.  AND IT NAMED THE SEAM INSTEAD OF THE REASON.  The
+            // backend knows why it declined and the receipt did not carry it;
+            // four cases in the 238 arm-A soak died with this exact sentence
+            // and nothing else.  Built only on the declining path, which was
+            // already about to run the whole CPU reconstruction loop.
+            std::string flatxs_why =
+                "the FlatXS device arm declined (" +
+                (_xsrecon_backend ? _xsrecon_backend->status()
+                                  : std::string("no backend")) +
+                "); the reference reconstruction loop runs";
+            RASBERY_GPU_FULL_GUARD_IF(rasberyGpuFlatXsEnabled() && !dump_this, FlatXs,
+                                      "XSSet::UpdateFlatXS", flatxs_why.c_str());
         }
     }
